# Lifecycle-script allowlist for npm installs in this project (#930).
#
# All Makefile npm installs run with `--ignore-scripts`, so no dependency
# install/build script runs. A package that genuinely needs its lifecycle
# scripts (for example, a native module that compiles at install time) is
# named here, one per line, with the reason in a comment above it. The install
# targets then run `npm rebuild` for exactly those packages.
#
# `make check` (scripts/check_npm_policy.py) fails if an entry does not name a
# package with an install script in package-lock.json, so stale entries cannot
# linger silently — remove an entry when the package goes away.
#
# Currently empty: every installed package works with its scripts disabled
# (esbuild finds its platform binary through the @esbuild/<platform> optional
# dependency; see docs/dependency-install-policy.md).
